A||||9||Superfiero||1/4 mile timeslips||||5||
Z||000000||Superfiero||03-25-2000||11:09 PM||||Just curious what kind of 1/4 mile times everyone is getting.  What kind of mods have been performed on car that netted these times?||||reg||5
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||03-26-2000||01:18 AM||||I went to the dragstrip with my 88 Coupe V6 last year. I pulled up to do a small burnout to clean the tires and practice my launch. There was way too much traction and I heard a loud "thunk". Turns out my tranny mount was about to explode, but I did run it anyway. I live in Utah and the elevation is about 4500 feet at RMR raceway. With a completey stock motor, a K&N filter, a Holley scoop and an Isuzu tranny.<P>I ran 4 times before I got put out. The first run was against a 99 Corba. This was a test run. The Cobra ran a 14.968@94.25 and I ran a 17.296@78.54. The second run I was alone... test run again... 17.316@78.61.<P>Now the actual racing started. I lined up with a 17.00 dial against a CRX with a 17.30 dial. He jumped me off the line, he hit a .463 and I woke up to a .930(i need to work on that) but I caught him. He ran a 17.418@79.00 and I ran a 17.053@76.90(I hit the brakes to avoid a break-out)... I won.<P>The second run was against another CRX. I lowered my dial to a 16.88 and he rolled up with a 16.85. I got left on the line again with a 1.110 and he hit a .631 light. 60 foot was 2.314(me) 2.678(him), 330 6.881(me) 7.166(him), 1/8 10.702@64.35(me) 10.856@66.66(him), 1000 foot 14.019(me) 14.086(him) 1/4 mile 16.966@74.11(me) 16.956@73.15(him). I hit the brakes hoping he would break-out and I would not break-out as bad. He had a few stickers all over his car, but not sure if he had any mods or not. I kinda took it easy on my car because of the tranny mount. I don't know how much faster I would have been if the mount wouldn't have failed.<P>I have ran my other Fiero(86SE w/a 4 spd) in Louisiana and constantly ran low 15's and once ran a 14.7@98 mph. I have the tranny mount fixed and added poly dogbone bushings and plan to go back when it opens later this year. Hoping for low 16's at this elevation and crappy gas (91 octane is the highest sold in Utah at the pumps).||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||03-27-2000||09:41 AM||||With the nitrous off my best times on DOT drag slicks is a 14.7. on street tires it's a 15.1. On the nitrous on street tires is 14.1. On nitrous with DOT drag tires on Panasport S/L 13.6@103. the following is the best street tire time... (still running the same tires) <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fierotime.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fierotime.jpg</A>  the car makes up for my weak RTs and 60' times. <BR><p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 03-27-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||88formula||03-27-2000||09:57 PM|||| 1FST2M6, You have to let me know what you did for mods, those time slips are amazing for a 2.8.||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||03-27-2000||11:26 PM||||How do you guys stage and do you launch at the last yellow or do you wait for green?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Superfiero||03-28-2000||12:46 AM||||Launch on the last yellow ||||reg||1
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||03-28-2000||12:51 AM||||I roll to the pre-stage then inch forward to clip the stage light and then take a nap. When I wakeup, the other guy is half way down the track  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I try to take off when the last yellow comes on.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Pretender||03-28-2000||02:13 AM||||my car 88GT AUTO. last season my best time was 15.83@ 86mph with a reaction time of .626. When i ran this time i had the power pully and power strip chip, Ocelot exhaust system with the straight pipe eliminating the cat. and a K&N air filter. The pass. seat and spare tire/jack were also removed. I cooled the intake down with a bag of ice while in the staging lanes. HighWay to the danger zone was on the radio at the time!(if that adds to the "rush" of racing.<P>This year i have upgrade the entire ing. system using a crane hi-6s box, ps-91 coil, 8.5mm wires(crane),bosch 4 plat. plugs, FOCOA headders w/ crosspipe, Crane adj. fuel pressure regulator, hypertech low temp switch, Custom cold air intake, redline water wetter for the coolant system. I'm also removing the entire a/c system. I want to run low 15's considering i spent about $1,000 if not more in these mods. I will be racing on april 22nd at mason dixion drag strip and hopefully i'll get my low 15's.  <P>When i stage i usually go around the water pit or wave the guy off so he doesn't spray my lane. I downshift to second gear, Line up till the second light goes on and stomp hard on my brake's. when mt opponate is finally done his/her burnout and lines up i start applying the gas. last yellow and i launch, my rpm's are around 1,700-2,000 and i keep it in second the entire way down the track. When i cross the line i'm redlining so as soon as i win/lose is shift to drive and coast the end of the track, Going to the end adds a  longer cool-down on the return lane. Sorry this is so long but it anwsers your questions. Talk to you guys L8r. Pretender.||||reg||10
Z||000008||1FST2M6||03-28-2000||09:30 AM||||Leave at the last yellow. Launch the car at 1300rpm... NOS or not. you can see a list of the mods I've done at  <A HREF="http://www.freeyellow.com/members/fiero/travis.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.freeyellow.com/members/fiero/travis.html</A>    that is most of the stuff done to the car... I've done some other things too.. I'll scan my best street tire no NOS run in a few.. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Dan86gt3.8||03-29-2000||04:22 AM||||I plan to go to the track sometime soon.  Tey just opened up a brand new one that about 30 min (at the most) away from my university, so hopefully I can go out SOOON!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
